<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="52727" href="schedule/2010/spring/LING/509/52727.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2010" href="schedule/2010.xml">2010</calendarYear><term id="120101" href="schedule/2010/spring.xml">Spring 2010</term><subject id="LING" href="schedule/2010/spring/LING.xml">Linguistics</subject><course id="509" href="schedule/2010/spring/LING/509.xml">Topics in Cognitive Ling</course></parents><sectionNumber>MT </sectionNumber><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Course Content:  The basic principles of cognitive linguistics (continuity of linguistic &amp; world knowledge, prototype structure, frame/schematic organization) are introduced and exemplified through the analysis of particular phenomena. In addition, issues in linguistic relativity, conceptual metaphor theories, Relevance Theory, and Construction Grammar(s) are discussed.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2010-01-19Z</startDate><endDate>2010-05-05Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>03:00 PM</start><end>05:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>W      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>1040</roomNumber><buildingName>Foreign Languages Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Terkourafi" firstName="M">Terkourafi, M</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>